Introduction
^^^^^^^^^^^^

Welcome to the fun, exciting world of arcade puzzling! This new, exciting
release by Monster Software combines all the action of an arcade game with
the mental stimulation of a puzzle game, providing hours of addictive,
relaxing entertainment. Or something like that anyway. This is the full
registered version of Stib, complete with five carefully graded levels, with
individual saved hiscore tables. See the end of this file for the licence
conditions.


Instructions
^^^^^^^^^^^^

On running the game you will be presented with a title screen. Choose a
difficulty level from the right-hand side (Practice is recommended to start
with) and click Play.

The main features of the playing screen are a grid of animated, colourful
but suicidal creatures ('Stibs'), and a firing device ('Stib shooter') at
the bottom centre. The Stib shooter is controlled using the mouse (it turns
left and right and can be fired with any of the mouse buttons).

The aim of the game is to eliminate all the Stibs from the playing area, for
reasons which are currently unclear. They each have a built-in self destruct
mechanism, but can only obtain enough power to activate it when they have
three or more neighbours of the same colour, and only when hit by a moving
Stib also of the same colour.

These explosions frequently lead to some of the other Stibs becoming
detached from the main group (which is always attached to the top of the
playing area), and if this happens they will fall off the playing area and
escape to safety (err, hang on, wasn't the aim of the game to kill them
all?). If, however, the group touches the firey lake at the bottom of the
screen, they will all be changed to evil demons (erm...) and your game will
be over.

To liven things up a bit, each time a Stib is fired the group becomes
increasingly unstable, indicated by a blue thermometer at the bottom of the
screen. They become critical when the thermometer fills up completely -
causing the entire playing area to permanently shift down a row. Do not
despair - when Stibs become detached, the thermometer goes down. The more
that fall off in one go, the more the thermometer decreases.


Scoring
^^^^^^^

You get 10 points for each Stib you shoot.
You get 30 points for each Stib exploded.
You get 60 points for each Stib detached.

Bonuses: You get 1000pts ◊ level number for completing a level. You also get
a bonus dependent on the number of Stibs used, which changes according to
the difficulty of the level.


Tints & Hips
^^^^^^^^^^^^

Once a type of Stib is eliminated, no more of that type will be given to
shoot. However, there is a slight delay caused by the ênext Stibë system
which makes things just a little bit tougher.

Stibs can be bounced off the side of the playing area. Be sure to check all
angles before you make unwise moves.

Once the level is nearly complete, it is advisable to êhangë Stibs off a
group of a different colour rather than the top of the screen. Youëll see
why if you try it. Similar tactics can be used earlier in the game, which is
especially useful on higher difficulty levels (which you as a privileged
registered user can play).


